n  marinade at the sella filet with about 1  TSP of olive oil salt and pepper quarter  teaspoon of chopped rosemary and one  minced garlic clove gently massage the  seasoning into the salmon and set aside  now let's prep the vegetables I've  sliced up about half a zucchini half a  cup of cherry tomatoes and half a lemon  line a baking tray with tinfoil then  make a bed for the salmon filet by  arranging all the vegetables on the  bottom and season with salt and pepper  then place the salmon and drizzle with  about two teaspoons of freshly squeezed  lemon juice still in all in tightly bake  in the oven until the salmon is cooked  through just for about 30 minutes enjoy  it hot each serving has about four  hundred and seventy calories this dish  is packed with omega-3 fatty acids from  the salmon and you're getting at least  two servings of vegetables what I really  like about this dish is that you can  prep a server ahead keep them in the  fridge and simply take them out and bake  them in the oven and the final recipe  has to be a veteran option my healthy  version of aubergine and black bean  ratatouille preheat the oven to 220  degrees Celsius let's prep the  vegetables slice up to aubergine and one  whole zucchini season them with 1 tbsp  of olive oil and salt and pepper toss  well for the sauce you'll need 1 can of  diced tomatoes 1 can of rinsed black  beans 1 chopped onion 2 diced garlic  cloves about quarter teaspoon of cayenne  pepper and salt and pepper to taste mix  all the ingredients together in a  separate bowl and set aside in a baking  dish a range of the aubergine and  zucchini slices in a single layer then  pour in a layer of black bean sauce top  it up with another  lair of aubergine and zucchini slices  repeat until the baking tray is filled  finally sprinkle with some grated cheese  bake in the oven for 30 to 40 minutes  until the top layer is golden brown  serve hearts each serving has about 240  calories if you're a vegan simply omit  the cheese